\
## Active Bugs (Do Not Close Without Fixing)\
\
### Bug A \'97 Intersection detection unreliable (most critical)\
fetchIntersectingRoads was recently rewritten to use a bounding-box Overpass\
query (instead of single-wayId node-sharing) to handle Cosgrove Ave being split\
into multiple OSM way segments. The fix is in place but NOT yet verified in the\
browser \'97 the user\'92s last screenshot still showed Personnel = 2 (no intersection\
detected). Possible remaining causes:\
- OSM data for the specific test location may not have the side road properly\
  node-connected\
- The nextNode branching check (minDistToPolylineLL(nextNode, polyline) <\
  CONN_DEG * 2) may be too aggressive, incorrectly classifying some true\
  intersections as continuations\
- The endpoint-only check may miss intersections where the junction is an\
  interior node of the side road (less common in OSM but possible)\
\
### Bug B \'97 T5-2 (stop/slow bat) count is always x2, never x3\
When an intersection CONTROLLER is generated, buildIntersectionTreatments adds\
T1-1 and T1-34 to signsOnSideRoad but NEVER adds a T5-2-stop for the controller\
standing at the junction with a bat. Fix is straightforward: add one T5-2-stop\
to signsOnSideRoad at distanceM: 0 for every CONTROLLER treatment. This is a\
one-line addition in buildIntersectionTreatments, NOT YET IMPLEMENTED.\
\
